## Per-ecosystem notes

- **vanilla** (data-attributes; provides: nothing — vanilla): Every Kineto module is available; there is no library component to defer to. Multi-page sites can add `data-kt-page-transition` on <body> for same-origin page transitions and `data-kt-page-reveal` for the first-paint overlay.
- **shadcn** (props-passthrough; provides: accordion, tabs, tooltip, toast, dialog, sheet, carousel, skeleton, progress, switch, navigation-menu, scroll-area): tw-animate-css (`animate-in`, `fade-in-0`, `zoom-in-95` …) already animates Dialog/Sheet/Popover content — do not add a Kineto reveal to the same node; animate the children instead. shadcn `Carousel` (Embla) owns the track; put Kineto reveal/tilt on the slides, never `data-kt-slider` on the same container. shadcn `Skeleton` is a layout placeholder; for images prefer `data-kt-lazy="skeleton"` on the `<img>` itself so the placeholder resolves into the real picture. Next.js App Router: the provider is a client component; server components can still render `data-kt-*` attributes. Tailwind v4 utilities and Kineto never fight over layout: Kineto only writes transform/opacity/filter/clip on the host and creates its own wrapper layers.
- **tailwind** (data-attributes; provides: nothing — vanilla): `animate-*` keyframe utilities and `transition-transform` on the same element as `data-kt-reveal`, `data-kt-gesture` or `data-kt-tilt` double-animate the host. daisyUI, Flowbite and Preline are plain class-based markup on top of Tailwind; everything in this entry applies to them.
- **bootstrap** (data-attributes; provides: accordion, collapse, tabs, tooltip, popover, toast, modal, offcanvas, carousel, placeholder, spinner, progress, dropdown, navbar): `.carousel` (Bootstrap) and `data-kt-slider` on the same element: choose one. Bootstrap carousel for content slides, Kineto slider when you want coverflow/cube/cards effects. `.placeholder` / `.placeholder-glow` and `data-kt-lazy="skeleton"`: choose one placeholder per image. `data-bs-toggle="tooltip"` and `data-kt-tooltip` on one element create two tooltips. `.accordion` (Bootstrap collapse) and `data-kt-accordion`: Bootstrap owns open/close; add Kineto reveal to the panel content instead. Bootstrap's `.fade` modal transition stays; animate the modal body with `data-kt-reveal` or `data-kt-text-split` for richer entrances. Bootstrap's grid and utilities are unaffected; Kineto never sets layout properties on the host.
- **mui** (props-passthrough; provides: accordion, tabs, tooltip, snackbar, dialog, drawer, skeleton, progress, switch, menu): MUI `Grow`/`Fade`/`Slide` transitions wrap Dialog and Menu content; do not add a Kineto reveal to the same node. MUI `ButtonBase` already renders a Material ripple (`TouchRipple`); use `data-kt-magnetic` or `data-kt-gesture` on buttons, not `data-kt-ripple`. Emotion class names are left untouched; Kineto writes inline styles it later restores on destroy.
- **mantine** (props-passthrough; provides: accordion, tabs, tooltip, notifications, modal, drawer, skeleton, progress, switch, carousel): `@mantine/carousel` (Embla) and `data-kt-slider` on one element: choose one. Mantine `Transition`/`Collapse` already animate their child; add Kineto to the content, not the transition node.
- **chakra** (props-passthrough; provides: accordion, tabs, tooltip, toaster, dialog, drawer, skeleton, progress, switch, menu): Chakra `Presence`/`Dialog` animate their positioner via `data-state` keyframes; do not add a Kineto reveal to the same node.
- **antd** (props-passthrough-or-wrapper; provides: collapse, tabs, tooltip, message, notification, modal, drawer, skeleton, progress, switch, carousel, dropdown): Ant Design `Carousel` (react-slick) and `data-kt-slider` on one element: choose one. `Statistic` has its own count-up animation when `formatter` uses CountUp; use either that or `data-kt-counter`, not both.
- **daisyui** (data-attributes; provides: skeleton, tooltip, tabs, collapse, toast, carousel, progress, modal, drawer): daisyUI `carousel` is CSS scroll-snap; `data-kt-slider` on the same element takes over the track — choose one. daisyUI `skeleton` boxes stay for text; use `data-kt-lazy="skeleton"` on images.
- **nuxt-ui** (attrs-fallthrough; provides: accordion, tabs, tooltip, toast, modal, slideover, skeleton, progress, switch, carousel, navigation-menu): Nuxt UI `UCarousel` (Embla) and `data-kt-slider`: choose one per container. Reka UI content nodes animate through `data-state`; add Kineto to their children. Components rendered on the server keep the attributes, so hydration sees the same markup the observer will scan.
- **primevue** (attrs-fallthrough; provides: accordion, tabs, tooltip, toast, dialog, sidebar, skeleton, progress, toggleswitch, carousel, galleria, megamenu): PrimeVue `Carousel`/`Galleria` and `data-kt-slider` on the same element: choose one. PrimeVue `Ripple` directive and `data-kt-ripple` on one button: choose one.
- **vuetify** (attrs-fallthrough; provides: expansion-panels, tabs, tooltip, snackbar, dialog, navigation-drawer, skeleton-loader, progress, switch, carousel, menu): `v-carousel` and `data-kt-slider` on one element: choose one. `v-btn` already has a ripple; use `data-kt-magnetic`/`data-kt-gesture` instead of `data-kt-ripple`.

## Option lookup

Exact option names, variants and defaults live in `kineto.features.json` (https://raw.githubusercontent.com/catgarret/kineto/main/kineto.features.json) and the generated reference (https://github.com/catgarret/kineto/blob/main/docs/module-reference.md). With the Kineto MCP server (`npx @dong-gri/kineto-mcp`) call `kineto_suggest`, `kineto_snippet` and `kineto_validate_options` instead of guessing.

## Do not generate these any more

| Instead of | Generate | Why |
|---|---|---|
| `data-kt-lazy="dither"` | `data-kt-stylize="dither"` | Lazy fetches an image; these redraw pixels that are already there. They are the Stylize module now, and Stylize adds the living look (motion, pointer) and the crisp dissolve reveal that the alias cannot reach. |
| `data-kt-lazy="ascii"` | `data-kt-stylize="ascii"` | Lazy fetches an image; these redraw pixels that are already there. They are the Stylize module now, and Stylize adds the living look (motion, pointer) and the crisp dissolve reveal that the alias cannot reach. |
| `data-kt-lazy="halftone"` | `data-kt-stylize="halftone"` | Lazy fetches an image; these redraw pixels that are already there. They are the Stylize module now, and Stylize adds the living look (motion, pointer) and the crisp dissolve reveal that the alias cannot reach. |

- Stylize does not load anything: use src, not data-src, and data-kt-mode="persist|reveal" instead of data-kt-persist. Both modules can sit on one element when the image also needs lazy loading.

The old markup keeps working until next major and emits a recoverable `KT_DEPRECATED` diagnostic when `debug` is on.

